The six attached files are reviewed; `executeTspSign` and the `procedure` base context are not attached, so their behavior remains open.

**Source-grounded review**

**Envelope-status guard**

When execution reaches L105 in `signEnvelopeFieldRoute` — after the recipient, field, version, assistant-SIGNATURE-field, field-type-match, and deleted-at guards have all passed — the route rejects if `envelope.status !== DocumentStatus.PENDING`.

```105:109:packages/trpc/server/envelope-router/sign-envelope-field.ts
    if (envelope.status !== DocumentStatus.PENDING) {
      throw new AppError(AppErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST, {
        message: `Document ${envelope.id} must be pending for signing`,
      });
    }
```

**Recipient already-signed guard**

When execution reaches L111 — after the envelope-status guard has passed — the route rejects if `recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED` OR `field.recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED`.

```111:115:packages/trpc/server/envelope-router/sign-envelope-field.ts
    if (recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED || field.recipient.signingStatus === SigningStatus.SIGNED) {
      throw new AppError(AppErrorCode.INVALID_REQUEST, {
        message: `Recipient ${recipient.id} has already signed`,
      });
    }
```

**Open questions**

1. Does the field lookup at L38–66 of `sign-envelope-field.ts` impose any envelope-status filter, making the status guard at L105–109 the sole rejection path for COMPLETED or REJECTED envelopes? A test calling `signEnvelopeFieldRoute` with a COMPLETED envelope and a valid non-ASSISTANT token would confirm which check fires first.

2. Does `executeTspSign` independently verify envelope status before embedding signatures, or does it rely solely on the guards in `signEnvelopeFieldRoute`? A doc comment or integration test on `executeTspSign` should specify whether it enforces a PENDING precondition independently.

3. Can `signingStatusEnvelopeRoute` return `PROCESSING` for an envelope whose `status` field is still `DocumentStatus.PENDING` — all recipients signed but envelope-level status not yet promoted to COMPLETED — and if so, is that transition window intentional? A doc note or test covering the ordering of recipient and envelope status updates would clarify the intended invariant.

